BT /F1 11 Tf 15 TL 50 685 Td
(QNX 4 uses an extent-based disk format designed for a real-time operating system.) Tj
T* (Unlike QNX6 Power-Safe, it has no alternate copy-on-write root transaction mechanism.) Tj
T* (Ordinary file metadata can live directly inside a directory entry, avoiding an) Tj
T* (additional inode lookup for short single-link names. Extended inode records support) Tj
T* (multiple names and longer names. Native metadata structures carry recognizable) Tj
T* (signatures to assist forensic reconstruction. The filesystem may occupy a whole floppy) Tj
T* (or a selected hard-disk partition; a partition type alone is not proof of valid media.) Tj
ET
