(The logical format uses 512-byte blocks regardless of host transfer geometry. On disk) Tj
T* (block addresses start at one; block b corresponds to partition-relative byte offset) Tj
T* (\(b-1\)*512. Zero is therefore not the first valid extent address. Physical block zero) Tj
T* (is the loader, physical block one the root block; the bitmap follows, then the root) Tj
T* (directory and remaining allocations. If the volume contains N complete 512-byte) Tj
T* (blocks, the bitmap needs ceil\(N/4096\) blocks. Check the root block's directory/inode) Tj
T* (records and special-file references independently. Host sector alignment must be) Tj
T* (handled by bounded byte I/O; never reinterpret a 4 KiB host block as one QNX4 block.) Tj
